% covers: 13 - in-place assign_index validates before it mutates, so a failed assignment leaves its target as it was (Scope); only the REPL survives an error to show it. A logical target refuses the NaN in [0 NaN] (02 spec, "A logical target refuses NaN") before writing the 0; y([1 1e300]) must fail growth before writing y(1)
x = true(1, 3);
x([1 2]) = [0 NaN]
disp(x)
y = [1 2 3];
y([1 1e300]) = 5
disp(y)
exit
